==Strategy==
This is an endurance stage with EVA Unit-13 and a cycle of peons, which are initially fast but slow down over time. Unlike [[Unit-13's False Evolution]], EVA Unit-13 is a Traitless enemy, although it still has a bunch of immunities meaning your Cannon of choice should either be the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]] or anything specifically for the peons. EVA Unit-13, like its Cat counterpart, has its hit split up into three multi-hits which occur quickly after each other, so its full 90,000 damage will only happen against extremely bulky units, or your base. Unlike its Cat counterpart, however, EVA Unit-13 has a low base range, but makes up for it with an Omni Strike up to 460 range, making it possible for you to use lower range units like Can Can against it.

Alone, EVA Unit-13 is easily stalled with units like Cat Cactus, Riceball or Stone Cat with good timing, so your main priority is chipping down each peon to allow your units to get damage knockbacks onto EVA Unit-13. Sir Seal is fairly easy to take care of, being a free moneybag killable with Can Can, Bullet Train, or Courier; Heavenly Hippoe can't really push much, just being a big wall of flesh. However, Shadow Boxer K and Aku Gory combined with EVA Unit-13 punishing leftover units can easily result in a loss if unprepared. For the former, a Talented Heavy Assault C.A.T or Pizza Cat alongside good Boulder Cat timing can take care of it. For the latter, you should use your Awakened Bahamut on him to not have to deal with his annoying Savage Blows. After the first two cycles of peons, the peons will die down severely, meaning at this point you should focus on killing EVA Unit-13. After maybe one or two more peon cycles, EVA Unit-13 should go down, and you can go on to win the stage. Do be careful of the anti-cheese present which has you fight all four supporting enemies though.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: An amazing option here, Stone is able to bait out hits from EVA Unit-13 or any of the supporting enemies. With three small Research Combos, Stone can permastall EVA Unit-13.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: With its True Form, Jelly Dumpling can now connect onto Sir Seal and Heavenly Hippoe, and unleash damaging Waves onto Shadow Boxer K as well.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]: An expensive option here, Cat Cactus neverthless has Surge Immune and can actually withstand hits from the peons unlike Gato Amigo. Also works against Aku Gory for good measure.
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]]: A fast meatshield who can become Slow Immune with Talents.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can can easily chip down Sir Seal and Heavenly Hippoe, farming the former for extra money, while it can also chip down EVA Unit-13 during the stage's downtime.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman is pretty useless for Shadow Boxer K and Aku Gory, but is great to chip down the boss.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Demolishes the Shadow Boxer K, but timing is needed to not get him Slowed and unable to attack from EVA Unit-13's Mini-Surges.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: A rusher who can demolish Heavenly Hippoe.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Alongside a Can Can hit, Courier can kill the Sir Seal and deal some generalist damage onto EVA Unit-13.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: A second Bullet Train who is only usable on EVA Unit-13.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: A powerful anti-Traitless nuker with damage comparable to D'arktanyan who can, with proper timing, remove tons of EVA Unit-13's health during its backswing.
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]]: A less accessible but better version of Pizza for this stage, their higher speed allows them to deal with Shadow Boxer K with greater consistency.
*Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: A powerful generalist who can unleash huge damage against any threat here.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: A disposable nuke button that can severely damage a supporting threat.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Even without his Talents, Bahamut alongside Stone timing can easily chain the Aku Gory to death and then get damage off on EVA Unit-13.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]]: Boasting the stats to be a helpful generalist as well as the range to outrange even EVA-13's omni, Newtone will put in the work to help you chip down the boss as well as any peons. His conjure can also be used as an emergency button to push back any enemies that gets too close to your base. Do be mindful that EVA-13's mini surge can actually hit Newtone, so be careful of that.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi]]: In his first form, Issun's high damage against Traitless makes him a great unit to quickly chip down EVA Unit-13.
*Rushers: Examples include [[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] and [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]. These units can rush to the frontline, get huge damage off, and then die, allowing the disposal of a supporting threat.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Balrog can activate his Strengthen from EVA Unit-13's hits, and then unleash crazy amounts of damage onto any supporting threat or EVA Unit-13 itself.
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]]: While neither Surge nor Slow Immune, D'arktanyan has high enough generalist stats to get good damage off on the supporting threats as well as Massive vs. Traitless for EVA Unit-13.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: Basically makes this stage free. Crits can one shot any support and deals boatloads of damage to EVA Unit-13. As a bonus, his range is even high enough for the surges to never hit him for enough damage to kill.

